WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.560
In ancient times,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:29.120
thousands of lions roamed freely across Africa.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:41.600
And prides living side by side.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.320
There is still a place like this,

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:53.760
where the raw forces of nature are in control.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.800
This is a kingdom where lions rule.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.360
A special breed,

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:49.200
hunters of giants.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:02:04.720
All mysteriously connected.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.640
Luaha,

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:13.840
the story of ancient Africa.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:31.520
The time of plenty is upon the land.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:42.240
It slows the heartbeat of&nbsp;
Africa and brings rain to Ruaha.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:48.640
This season has the power to transform.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.920
To dilute,

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:58.000
to disarm.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:06.560
This season has the power to restore.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.640
But none of the water that fills the rivers can

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:33.680
wash away what happened here.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:59.360
It
began in the dry season.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.280
In a bend in the Mwagusi River,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.800
even during the hottest,

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.480
driest summer,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.440
there is always water here.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.760
In a place called the Glade,

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.520
it is a sanctuary.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.040
It is a haven,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:29.440
the essence of life for all the animals of Ruaha.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:47.280
But nothing is quite as it seems.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:52.720
Strange things happen here.

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:56.640
Strange alliances.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.640
In the natural world,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:11.120
lions hunt baboons.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.000
In the glade,

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.360
however,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:23.680
generations of lion and baboon&nbsp;
families have coexisted.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.840
A small pride of lions currently lives here.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.880
Two wise old lionesses and their cubs.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:48.960
Life is charmed.

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.040
Oh.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:30.560
The Glade Pride follows the rules&nbsp;
set down by their forebears.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:41.520
Never touch the baboons.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.840
There's a reason for this.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.840
There's nothing more dangerous than

00:06:59.840 --> 00:07:08.320
a hungry lion.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.520
Kudu,

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.320
drawn to the glade to drink.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:24.720
Scatter in a heartbeat if they hear the alarm.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.360
Usually,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.760
baboons cry out when danger threatens,

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:34.880
but not in the glade.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:35.440
Here,

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.960
they abandon their posts to follow danger.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:50.560
In complete silence,

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:56.400
the kudu listen for a warning call.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:03.840
Silence signals safe passage.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.400
And so,

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:26.480
the kudu enter the kill zone.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.280
Not a sound.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.040
And all the while,

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:38.640
she steals closer.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:47.120
Last chance to warn.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:56.480
Betrayal is complete.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:12.480
The glade pride will eat well today,

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:20.320
thanks to the baboons.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:20.800
Why,

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.120
against all natural instincts,

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:35.040
do these baboons remain silent when lions prowl?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:39.680
What's in it for the baboons?

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.520
If a hungry lion is a dangerous lion,

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.440
a lion with a full belly is a safer lion.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.440
Keep the glade pride fed,

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:56.160
and there may be peace between natural enemies.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:10:13.280
It could be as simple as that.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:29.760
And so it is in this bend in the river,

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.160
called the Glade,

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:42.640
a very special place.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.640
But trouble is on the way.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:53.360
Massive herds of buffalo forced to leave&nbsp;
the parched highlands in search of water.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:11:09.280
Are being drawn like magnets to the glade.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.680
The buffalo collective is

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:12.720
a thirsty,

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:24.960
sprawling mass of brawn and horn.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:33.600
They're being shadowed by&nbsp;
an unusual pride of lions.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.640
The Unja,

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.120
Buffalo Soldier,

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.320
aggressive,

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.760
unpredictable,

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.960
worthy of respect.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.280
The injar have their measure.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:58.160
They are in tune with the nature of the herd.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:03.600
Their territory is boundless&nbsp;
because it's constantly on the move.

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:27.440
The injar pride consider the&nbsp;
buffalo to be their territory.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:32.880
The Anjar have perfected the&nbsp;
dark art of the buffalo kill.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.760
They
seek the vulnerable.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:13:00.400
Hidden at the heart of this herd&nbsp;
are the young and the injured.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:15.200
The injar will weed them out.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:22.480
An injured calf.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:27.120
Target locked.

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:39.600
Push the soldiers forward.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:48.160
Spirit the young one away&nbsp;
under cloak of shadow and dust.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:55.600
They make it look easy.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.160
An injured calf's misfortune.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:05.760
One less to slow the buffalo down.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:16.960
The herd grows stronger.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:25.200
Would they march onward to the&nbsp;
glade in the heat of the day?

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:30.960
The injah never far behind.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:32.000
The injah,

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:37.520
a lean and mean.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.840
Power-hungry drifters.

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:43.760
They have taken the vulnerable from the herd.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:51.360
Now they will take on the soldiers.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:15:16.320
Oh.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:34.960
The
injar live off the buffalo.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:46.080
This herd belongs to them.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:16:00.400
A
cheetah is watching the injars herd,

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:13.280
but she is not interested in the buffalo.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.360
She's looking for hangers-on,

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:19.040
impala that shadow the herd,

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:26.960
masked behind a veil of false security.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:30.320
A superb hunter and a mother,

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:33.520
she is a cheetah in lion country,

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:37.440
where cubs rarely survive.

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:40.480
So far,

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:55.200
she's raised three.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:58.160
Risk of lion attack on her family is

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.800
great.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:18.320
Hunger drives the cheetah on.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:23.120
She has a long way to travel before she can hunt.

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:26.320
The impala will soon abandon the plains,

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:28.320
together with the buffalo,

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:32.080
all on the same journey.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.560
Drawn to the last waters of the glade,

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.800
one thirsty buffalo herd,

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.960
six hundred strong,

00:17:52.960 --> 00:18:02.880
shadowed by the inja.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.800
Always on the move,

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:07.040
cubs in tow.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:14.320
The injar will follow the&nbsp;
buffalo wherever they take them,

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.160
even into other lions'

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.080
territories.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:26.600
They are the injar.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:35.520
Guardians of the gates of the glade,

00:18:35.520 --> 00:18:39.760
an ancient forest of baobab trees.

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.640
Some have survived hundreds of years,

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:46.640
standing witness to the&nbsp;
change of countless seasons.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:08.320
Baobab forest provides for all.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:10.560
There is great power here.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:23.760
This forest is the territory of the&nbsp;
biggest lion pride in all of Ruaha.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:28.080
The Baobab pride.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:30.400
More than thirty members,

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:33.040
numbers far above the ordinary,

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:38.160
powerful lioness hunters and their offspring,

00:19:45.920 --> 00:20:03.600
and the baobab forest provides&nbsp;
for every one of them.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:23.840
The first buffalo herd of the dry&nbsp;
season arrives in the Baobab forest.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:26.960
This is not the Injara pride's buffalo.

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:31.280
This herd has come from the north.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:44.800
Over a thousand strong,

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:51.440
the babar pride relies on the&nbsp;
annual arrival of the buffalo.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:52.640
But this time,

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:55.520
the herd is not stopping in the forest.

00:20:56.800 --> 00:21:06.240
Thirst drives the parched buffalo&nbsp;
on to the waters of the glade.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.800
If the beaupré pride follows,

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.880
they will leave their forest,

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:14.720
trespass into the glade pride's territory.

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:19.440
Forbidden territory.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.440
Unable to resist the&nbsp;
temptation of hunting buffalo,

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:35.680
they leave the safety of their sanctuary.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:55.520
Glade pride lionesses have witnessed the&nbsp;
arrival of the buffalo countless times.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:22:03.440
It's been many months since the grunt and grind&nbsp;
of the great herds last shattered their peace.

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:15.440
But this time,

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:24.480
something is different.

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:33.200
The sound of too many hooves,

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:46.160
heading from opposite directions.

00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:51.680
Two herds of buffalo are marching on the glade.

00:22:55.440 --> 00:23:08.960
The one herd from the baobab forest,

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:10.560
from the west,

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:20.320
the injars herd.

00:23:20.320 --> 00:23:25.600
It's not the masses of thirsty&nbsp;
beasts that concern the glade pride.

00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:28.320
It's what follows.

00:23:28.320 --> 00:23:34.080
It's their own kind they fear,

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:38.560
a threat to their cubs.

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:40.240
Just a small pride,

00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:45.680
but wise mothers many times over.

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:51.920
The old lionesses know from experience&nbsp;
that behind all that dust and noise,

00:23:51.920 --> 00:23:54.160
other lions follow.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:24:01.600
With a lust to kill,

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:05.200
the family must leave its paradise for now.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:07.040
They will be back,

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:12.160
but not before peace returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:20.400
under the false protection of the buffalo.

00:24:20.400 --> 00:24:31.520
The impala are delivered&nbsp;
to the waters of the glade.

00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:37.840
Desperation delivers the cheetahs.

00:24:37.840 --> 00:24:40.880
The mother cheetah must make a kill.

00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:52.640
Her hungry cubs depend on it.

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:57.920
To hunt in a lion pride's&nbsp;
territory is to invite attack.

00:24:57.920 --> 00:24:58.560
Right now,

00:24:58.560 --> 00:25:02.000
she has a narrow window of opportunity,

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:10.480
because the glade pride is not here,

00:25:10.480 --> 00:25:12.640
but the baboons are.

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:14.320
And if they spot her,

00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:16.800
they will raise the alarm.

00:25:16.800 --> 00:25:20.000
She must wait for the impala to drink.

00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:25.760
To move away from the baboons.

00:25:25.760 --> 00:25:28.880
Hunger pushes a cub forward.

00:25:28.880 --> 00:25:34.080
Threatens their cover.

00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:39.760
The act,

00:25:39.760 --> 00:25:56.560
unseen.

00:25:56.560 --> 00:25:58.720
No more risks.

00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:00.720
The cubs must stay.

00:26:00.720 --> 00:26:03.200
Learn this lesson from afar.

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:05.040
A life lesson.

00:26:05.040 --> 00:26:06.320
A quick kill,

00:26:06.320 --> 00:26:24.320
to survive.

00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:49.120
The baboons will decide who kills here.

00:26:49.120 --> 00:26:51.360
The cheetah retreats.

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:53.840
She's not geared for combat.

00:26:54.560 --> 00:27:16.160
The baboons will send poachers&nbsp;
back to where they came from.

00:27:16.160 --> 00:27:22.240
A successful kill would have meant&nbsp;
life for a family of cheetahs.

00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:25.680
Still,

00:27:25.680 --> 00:27:32.160
she breathes in the shadow of a&nbsp;
creature with dubious motives,

00:27:32.160 --> 00:27:39.840
ally of the glade lions.

00:27:39.840 --> 00:28:04.880
Is this curiosity or concern?

00:28:04.880 --> 00:28:06.507
Oh,

00:28:06.507 --> 00:28:08.134
oh,

00:28:08.133 --> 00:28:09.760
oh.

00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:16.000
Even they are surprised when&nbsp;
she springs back to life.

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:19.760
The baboons expelled a poacher.

00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:28.320
Their intervention has saved a life.

00:28:34.160 --> 00:28:46.400
Strange things happen in the glade.

00:28:57.600 --> 00:29:02.880
The herd from the Bayabab&nbsp;
forest floods into the riverbed.

00:29:02.880 --> 00:29:15.920
The pathfinders lead them&nbsp;
into the heart of the glade.

00:29:21.120 --> 00:29:24.000
Perfect storm,

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:31.840
as the injars herd descends&nbsp;
on the very same water,

00:29:31.840 --> 00:29:40.480
and two mighty buffalo herds become one.

00:29:58.160 --> 00:30:01.040
They come with a thirst that will only be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:01.040 --> 00:30:07.520
conquered when every last&nbsp;
buffalo has had its fill.

00:30:13.040 --> 00:30:16.400
Confrontation with the enemy is inevitable,

00:30:16.400 --> 00:30:19.920
but the outcome is not,

00:30:19.920 --> 00:30:26.240
because now their force has doubled.

00:30:26.240 --> 00:30:29.600
The babar pride arrives in the glade,

00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:34.720
trespasses in the forbidden territory.

00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:41.440
Temptation,

00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:43.120
too great.

00:30:43.120 --> 00:30:45.840
Their fate is sealed.

00:30:45.840 --> 00:30:49.760
They will hunt in the glade,

00:30:49.760 --> 00:30:53.840
search for weak spots.

00:30:53.840 --> 00:30:55.600
Split up.

00:30:55.600 --> 00:31:00.960
Wait for the right moment to attack.

00:31:11.120 --> 00:31:13.920
The soldiers sense impending danger,

00:31:13.920 --> 00:31:23.120
lurking somewhere in the sands.

00:31:30.400 --> 00:31:38.880
Break cover.

00:31:38.880 --> 00:31:46.400
Create a stampede.

00:32:02.320 --> 00:32:12.800
Probe for weakness.

00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:18.720
Split

00:32:18.720 --> 00:32:21.200
the herd.

00:32:21.200 --> 00:32:41.040
Drive them out of the riverbed.

00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:42.080
A
mistake.

00:32:42.960 --> 00:32:54.560
Trapped.

00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:57.040
Buffalo,

00:32:57.040 --> 00:33:07.280
take it to the lions.

00:33:37.760 --> 00:33:38.000
Oh.

00:33:38.000 --> 00:33:51.520
Bea-Bab lions have made two fundamental errors.

00:33:51.520 --> 00:33:52.800
They chose to hunt in.

00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:55.600
In the hottest part of the day,

00:33:55.600 --> 00:34:01.840
and they attack the buffalo&nbsp;
before they'd finished drinking.

00:34:01.840 --> 00:34:15.200
Belligerent buffalo can take the&nbsp;
heat and will fight to drink.

00:34:15.200 --> 00:34:28.400
How long can the lions hold position?

00:34:34.160 --> 00:34:48.320
One determined young lioness still&nbsp;
has the energy to test the herd.

00:34:57.840 --> 00:35:09.280
This could be the first and&nbsp;
last buffalo she ever attacks.

00:35:16.880 --> 00:35:20.160
In
the heart of forbidden territory,

00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:21.040
hungry,

00:35:21.040 --> 00:35:22.080
hot,

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:23.440
exhausted,

00:35:23.440 --> 00:35:26.880
hopes of bounty evaporating fast.

00:35:26.880 --> 00:35:33.440
The Beababs have given all they have to give,

00:35:33.440 --> 00:35:36.880
but there is more to come.

00:35:42.720 --> 00:35:46.160
The Anjar pride has arrived,

00:35:46.160 --> 00:35:54.960
and they don't like what they see.

00:35:54.960 --> 00:36:03.040
A large pride of strange lions&nbsp;
is holding their buffalo at bay.

00:36:10.080 --> 00:36:13.040
The injar is not the biggest pride,

00:36:13.040 --> 00:36:18.560
but these lions are ferocious.

00:36:18.560 --> 00:36:23.200
A babab lioner spots the injar entering the glade.

00:36:23.200 --> 00:36:28.160
There is nothing but pure&nbsp;
foreboding in their advance.

00:36:28.160 --> 00:36:28.640
Now,

00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:39.040
two prides in the forbidden territory.

00:36:39.040 --> 00:36:45.280
Baab Bab lionesses on alert.

00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:50.640
Nja in position.

00:36:50.640 --> 00:36:54.080
A young Anjar male breaks the ranks.

00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:56.800
Instinct drives him forward.

00:36:56.800 --> 00:37:20.160
His first encounter with&nbsp;
female strangers in the flesh.

00:37:20.160 --> 00:37:24.880
Baabab lionesses challenge his insolence.

00:37:28.400 --> 00:37:38.240
An adult male would never&nbsp;
tolerate a lioness's defiance,

00:37:38.240 --> 00:37:43.280
but there are no adult males here.

00:37:43.280 --> 00:37:49.680
Lionesses dominate both prides.

00:37:49.680 --> 00:37:54.240
And the injar leader is the most&nbsp;
powerful lioness of them all.

00:38:07.120 --> 00:38:09.520
There can be no retreat.

00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:16.880
Every member of both prides&nbsp;
will have to fight this battle.

00:38:16.880 --> 00:38:21.280
Their futures are at stake.

00:38:35.040 --> 00:38:46.400
The
buffalo sense it.

00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:47.760
The glade,

00:38:47.760 --> 00:38:50.080
giver of life,

00:38:50.080 --> 00:39:07.200
is about to become an arena of war.

00:39:30.400 --> 00:39:30.480
Oh.

00:39:44.480 --> 00:39:50.480
The
injar have the edge.

00:39:50.480 --> 00:39:51.840
Beaube Pride,

00:39:51.840 --> 00:39:55.360
the largest pride in all of Ruaha,

00:39:55.360 --> 00:40:04.320
driven out of the glade.

00:40:04.320 --> 00:40:10.160
But there are worse things than being beaten.

00:40:10.160 --> 00:40:14.480
One of their own has been left behind.

00:40:14.480 --> 00:40:15.760
The young.
Young Linus,

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:19.120
who tried to prove her worth as a buffalo hunter,

00:40:19.120 --> 00:40:30.720
has been taken hostage by the injah.

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:56.160
They
could kill her right now.

00:40:56.160 --> 00:40:57.280
Instead,

00:40:57.280 --> 00:40:59.360
they torture.

00:40:59.360 --> 00:41:11.680
Her cries of suffering stop&nbsp;
the bayabab pride's retreat.

00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:14.560
The defeated watch and listen.

00:41:14.560 --> 00:41:25.680
As the torment continues.

00:41:51.200 --> 00:41:55.040
There is only one way to stop the torture.

00:41:55.040 --> 00:42:08.560
The bear bab pride must submit to the inja.

00:42:08.560 --> 00:42:22.960
The lions must return to the battleground.

00:42:34.000 --> 00:42:36.480
The bayabab pride leader could

00:42:36.480 --> 00:42:39.040
be entering a trap.

00:42:39.040 --> 00:42:39.520
Still,

00:42:39.520 --> 00:42:42.800
she goes forward.

00:42:42.800 --> 00:42:48.480
To stop the pain,

00:42:48.480 --> 00:43:01.520
alone she stands to put an end&nbsp;
to the lioness's suffering.

00:43:01.520 --> 00:43:11.920
The bear Babliya lays down in complete&nbsp;
submission before her Njarka counterpart.

00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:16.560
Too late for bravado.

00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:24.640
The injah have what they want.

00:43:24.640 --> 00:43:27.840
They've taught the beabab pride a lesson.

00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:33.360
Stay away from their buffalo.

00:43:33.360 --> 00:43:39.360
The beababs have their lioness back.

00:43:39.360 --> 00:43:44.560
Her injuries are severe.

00:43:44.560 --> 00:43:45.760
Can she stand?

00:43:51.360 --> 00:43:53.200
Defeated by battle,

00:43:53.200 --> 00:43:55.360
and now by heat,

00:43:55.360 --> 00:44:01.680
the pride moves off to the&nbsp;
edge of the glade to wait.

00:44:01.680 --> 00:44:06.800
Give the injured lioness a chance.

00:44:09.760 --> 00:44:14.640
The fearless leader risked her&nbsp;
life to submit to the injar.

00:44:14.640 --> 00:44:27.440
All in vain.

00:44:27.440 --> 00:44:32.160
The heat is sucking up the&nbsp;
last energy in the glade.

00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:35.120
The leader has no choice.

00:44:36.560 --> 00:44:40.240
Time for the pride to return to their territory,

00:44:40.240 --> 00:44:53.840
the Beabab forest.

00:45:04.320 --> 00:45:08.560
Torn between the pride and&nbsp;
the bond with her daughter,

00:45:08.560 --> 00:45:22.400
the mother is the last to go.

00:45:33.600 --> 00:45:43.520
She stayed as long as she can,

00:45:51.200 --> 00:46:04.240
but
it's the heat that drives her away.

00:46:04.240 --> 00:46:53.760
Oh,
oh,

00:46:53.760 --> 00:47:06.800
Last breath taken in the glade.

00:47:17.520 --> 00:47:33.280
Nothing can change what happened in these sands.

00:47:46.800 --> 00:48:02.800
Buffalo now drink their fill in&nbsp;
the golden hours of the glade.

00:48:07.920 --> 00:48:09.120
Fortunes

00:48:09.120 --> 00:48:17.040
change.

00:48:17.040 --> 00:48:32.160
Life is taken and given again.

00:48:35.440 --> 00:48:53.120
The glade lionesses return with their cubs.

00:48:53.120 --> 00:48:54.720
Her body,

00:48:54.720 --> 00:48:59.640
all that's left to show what happened here.

00:48:59.640 --> 00:49:00.640
Oh.

00:49:00.640 --> 00:49:29.040
Oh.

00:49:32.720 --> 00:49:55.360
A young stranger.

00:49:59.760 --> 00:50:13.440
There's
a lesson here.

00:50:14.480 --> 00:50:18.160
Awaken,

00:50:19.040 --> 00:50:22.080
more powerful strangers,

00:50:22.080 --> 00:50:24.720
formidable hunters,

00:50:24.720 --> 00:50:38.160
on their way to the glade.

